{
  "meta": {
    "title": "The Peak Is Coming — 8 billion, and the line that bends back",
    "id": "the-peak",
    "aspect": "16:9",
    "fps": 30,
    "duration": 88,
    "design": "vox-editorial",
    "x_note": "Fifth film, fifth design language: VOX editorial. The first film whose subject IS the data, so it is the first to use the chart element: six graphics across eight scenes. Every number is a published UN World Population Prospects 2024 figure; NOTES.md lists each one against its source so the film can be checked rather than believed. Fonts are the free stand-ins for VOX's licensed Balto / Alright Sans — see Design.md §2."
  },

  "design": {
    "style": "vox editorial",
    "x_note": "One theme. VOX's identity is a single flat field carrying one saturated yellow, so a light variant would be a different publication rather than the same one dimmed.",
    "tokens": {
      "bg": "#0e1012",
      "surface": "#171a1c",
      "surface-hi": "#22282b",
      "on-surface": "#f1f3f2",
      "on-variant": "#a3a8a6",
      "outline": "#3d4346",
      "outline-var": "#2b3134",
      "brand": "#ffeb00",
      "brand-warm": "#ffb020",
      "on-brand": "#141414",
      "brand-deep": "#35313f",
      "series-1": "#ffeb00",
      "series-2": "#7cc4ff",
      "series-3": "#ff7a59",
      "series-4": "#7bdcb5",
      "series-5": "#c9a6ff",
      "series-6": "#e8eae9",
      "grid": "#2e3437"
    },
    "theme_map": {
      "panel": "surface",
      "ink": "on-surface",
      "on-variant": "on-variant",
      "meter": "brand",
      "meter-track": "surface-hi",
      "accent": "brand",
      "num-a": "brand",
      "num-b": "brand-warm",
      "slab-ink": "on-brand",
      "fill": "brand",
      "fill-ink": "on-brand",
      "fill-tone": "surface",
      "outline": "outline",
      "s1": "series-1",
      "s2": "series-2",
      "s3": "series-3",
      "s4": "series-4",
      "s5": "series-5",
      "s6": "series-6",
      "chart-grid": "grid"
    },
    "theme_map_note": "The six series roles are the point of the chart work: a categorical palette belongs to the design language, not to one chart. They are declared as TOKENS here so the film states its five colours once and every graphic draws from them — and so a second mode would swap the whole set with one flag instead of hunting for hand-picked hexes inside forty bars.",
    "fills": {
      "card": "filled",
      "tiles": "tonal",
      "pills": "outlined",
      "answer": "text"
    },
    "fills_note": "`answer` is `text` because the closing line is a sentence, not a box — VOX's editorial graphics do not put the takeaway in a container, they just set it larger. `card` is `filled` so a headline number reverses out of the yellow block, which is the one visual move that reads as this publication.",
    "radii": {
      "pill": "999px",
      "card": "4px",
      "tile": "4px",
      "answer": "0"
    },
    "radii_note": "Nearly square. A 20px card radius is Material's language, and using it here would make a VOX graphic look like an Android screen.",
    "fonts": {
      "display": {
        "family": "Archivo",
        "weight": 800,
        "usage": "headlines. Stand-in for Balto — Archivo is a grotesque with the same narrow, high-contrast capitals and a real 800 weight, which Balto's own headline cut has and most free grotesques do not."
      },
      "overline": {
        "family": "JetBrains Mono",
        "weight": 700
      },
      "body": {
        "family": "Libre Franklin",
        "weight": 400,
        "usage": "standfirsts and captions. Stand-in for Alright Sans, which descends from Franklin Gothic — Libre Franklin is the closest open relative."
      },
      "lead": {
        "family": "Libre Franklin",
        "weight": 400
      },
      "mono": {
        "family": "JetBrains Mono",
        "weight": 500
      },
      "stat": {
        "family": "Archivo",
        "weight": 800
      }
    },
    "font_href": "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@400;500;600;700;800;900&family=Libre+Franklin:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&display=swap",
    "radius": "4px",
    "border": "1px solid #3d4346",
    "background": {
      "type": "flat",
      "base": "#0e1012"
    },
    "text_width": {
      "lead": 1280,
      "body": 1240
    },
    "text_width_note": "A chart is deliberately NOT capped here: it gets an explicit max_width per element instead, because a graphic wants the full measure of the stage and a paragraph does not."
  },

  "frame": {
    "design_space": { "w": 1920, "h": 1080 },
    "safe": { "title": 0.05, "action": 0.03, "max_text_width": 1280 },
    "ramp": {
      "overline": { "family": "JetBrains Mono", "size": 22, "weight": 700, "tracking": "0.2em", "case": "upper" },
      "title": { "family": "Archivo", "size": 104, "weight": 800, "tracking": "-0.03em" },
      "title_hi": { "family": "Archivo", "size": 62, "weight": 800, "tracking": "-0.02em" },
